# Local test/run artifacts
results/
*.log
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Compiled collector output - these are built by velociraptor/Build-Collector.ps1
# (or manually) and are large, environment-specific binaries, never source content.
# A real one landed in velociraptor/ once during testing - this prevents a repeat.
*.exe
NewCollector.zip
*-collector.zip
# Extracted collector output. A real collection is TENS OF GIGABYTES - a
# 17GB one here stalled `git add` outright - and it is evidence, which has no
# business in a public repo. The .zip above is covered; this is the folder it
# unpacks to.
*-collector/
throwaway-server.config.yaml
# Fetched at collector-build time from triage.velocidex.com by
# Build-Collector.ps1 / New-CaseCollector.ps1 - a downloaded upstream
# artifact, deliberately not vendored, so it stays current.
velociraptor/Windows.Triage.Targets.yaml

# Terraform - state files (which contain real resource IDs/values and the
# generated Windows admin password - see infra/SECURITY.md) and
# working-directory artifacts never belong in git. This covers per-case
# workspace state too: terraform.tfstate.d/ matches *.tfstate.* below.
#
# Note .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored - provider lock
# files are meant to be committed, so a partner org cloning this gets the
# same provider versions these modules were validated against.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
# Local variable values (e.g. the shared Bastion's VNet ID / subnet CIDR,
# written by Start-CloudConsole.ps1 option [8]) - environment-specific, not
# shared config. *.tfvars.example stays tracked if one is ever added.
*.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Local, non-secret case bookkeeping (case IDs, regions, resource names) -
# see infra/README.md's "Accounts, tokens, and secrets" section. Never
# contains credential material, but is still local-only, not shared state.
infra/.cases/

# Which shared network / tools storage this machine created, so the console
# can offer them as defaults. Same rule as above: bookkeeping, never secrets,
# but specific to one operator's cloud accounts and not shared state.
infra/.prereqs.json
